    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math learning by adapting to individual student needs, offering step-by-step explanations for tricky topics, and providing instant feedback on practice problems. They can also create engaging, interactive lessons that make abstract concepts more relatable. This helps students learn at their own pace without feeling overwhelmed."
